{
	title: 'Source modules stay under 400 lines',
	description: 'No non-test source module under src/ (.ts or .tsx) is longer than 400 lines (as wc -l counts them), so every module fits one read and has one job. src/conventions.test.ts enforces it and names each offender with its line count. A short list in that test allows exceptions, each with a one-line reason; normally it holds only src/common/ason.ts (one cohesive format: its parser and stringifier belong together). While a planned split has not landed, an oversized file may sit on the list with the task that splits it as its reason (src/host/host.ts: yq, src/client/frame.ts: 3m, src/web/page.ts: 1b); those tasks take their entry off. A listed file that is no longer over the limit, or no longer exists, fails the test, so the list never goes stale. Tests (*.test.ts) have no limit. Record the rule in tasks/README.md (Layout and module conventions).',
	status: 'done',
